    "title": "Police investigate false threat reported at Auburn University - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Drew Taylor No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nBIRMINGHAM, Ala. ( WIAT ) — A false threat reported to police led to police briefly evacuating the area near the Ralph B. Draughon Library at Auburn University while they searched the area.\nAU’s Campus Safety team sent out a social media post after 5:30 p.m. Wednesday to warn people to avoid the area near the library due to a “heavy police presence.” At the time, no other details were given.\nNo cameras captured situation involving severely injured student, Tuscumbia superintendent says However, by 5:48 p.m., the university had announced that police had cleared the area and that there was no active threat to the community.\n“Auburn Police immediately responded to a false report of a possible threat on campus,” a statement from AU read. : Following a thorough search, authorities determined there was no threat to the Auburn University community.”\nThe threat came hours after a shooting at Annunciation Catholic School in Minneapolis , where two children were killed and 14 others injured.\nNo other details on the threat have been released. The case remains under investigation.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHNT.com.",
